##* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess| chapter=The Elopers| page=33| passage=The huge square '''box''', parquet-floored and high-ceilinged, had been arranged to display a suite of bedroom furniture designed and made in the halcyon days of the last quarter of the nineteenth century, when modish taste was just due to go clean out of fashion for the best part of the next hundred years.}}
