##* {{quote-book|en|author=John Crossingham|chapter=The Essentials” and “Goaltending|editor=Bobbie Kalman| title=Lacrosse in Action| series=Sports in Action| location=New York, N.Y.; St. Catharines, Ont.| publisher=Crabtree Publishing Company| year=2003| pages=12 and 30| pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ShXWncCpluMC&pg=PA12| isbn=978-0-7787-0329-7| passage=&#91;[https://books.google.com/books?id=ShXWncCpluMC&pg=PA12 page 12]&#93; Field players wear shoes with short spikes, called ''cleats'', on the soles. '''Box''' players wear ''court shoes'', which have grooved rubber soles. {{...}} &#91;[https://books.google.com/books?id=ShXWncCpluMC&pg=PA30 page 30]&#93; Field goalies have larger nets to protect than goalies in box lacrosse have. '''Box''' goalies wear more pads. }}
